<title>UK: UK's Labour has no wish to raise VAT - Brown.</title>
<headline>UK's Labour has no wish to raise VAT - Brown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Opposition Labour's finance spokesman Gordon Brown said on Tuesday the party had no desire to raise value-added tax if it wins the next election.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no wish to put up VAT,&quot; Brown told reporters at a London news conference.  </p>
<p>He said there was nothing in Labour's programme which required such a move.</p>
<p>Labour leader Tony Blair added that Labour was the party that had most recently secured a tax cut in Britain by ensuring the ruling Conservatives could not go ahead with a second increase of VAT on fuel.</p>
<p>-- Anthony Williams +44 171 542 7715</p>
